          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Under mild conditions, a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi T
                  %msup
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subset T Alg^{op}
            of formal duals of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+Lawvere+theory"} algebras over an algebraic theory
            admits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} Isbell duality
            exhibited by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %msup
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi Δ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi Spec
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi 𝒪
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\mathcal{O} \dashv Spec) : (T Alg^{\Delta})^{op} \stackrel{\overset{\mathcal{O}}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{Spec}{\to}}
                  Sh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
          %p
            as described at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+algebras+on+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} function algebras on ∞-stacks
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            is an
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This entry describes for certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+stacks"} algebraic stacks
            an analog of this situation where the 1-algebras are replaced by 2-algebras in the form of commutative algebra objects in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+categories"} abelian categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+categories"} symmetric monoidal categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            are replaced with category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC(X)
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaves"} quasicoherent sheaves
          %p
            The replacement of the 1-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}(X)
            by the 2-algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC(X)
            is the starting point for what is called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+noncommutative+geometry"} derived noncommutative geometry
          %h2#setup Setup
          %h3#ringed_toposes Ringed toposes
          %p
            All
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+topos"} ringed topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S, \mathcal{O}_S)
            is a topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            equipped with a ring object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_S
            – a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            of rings – called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            – on whatever
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            on. We write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi S
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_S Mod
            for the category of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            (sheaves of modules) over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_S
          %p
            We write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi RngdTopos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RngdTopos
            for the category of ringed toposes.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            or more generally an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+stack"} algebraic stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi et
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X_{et})
            for its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+etale+topos"} little etale topos
          #localWRTEtaleTopology.un_def
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A ringed topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\mathcal{O}_S)
              is a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+topos"} locally ringed topos
              with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+topology"} étale topology
              if for every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in S
              and every family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Spec
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi Spec
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{Spec R_i \to Spec \mathcal{O}_S(U)\}
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphism"} étale morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O}_S(U) \to \prod_i R_i
            %p
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithfully+flat"} faithfully flat
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_i \to E
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and factorizations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_S(U) \to R_i \to  \mathcal{O}_S(E_i)
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\coprod_i E_i \to E
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} enough points
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S, \mathcal{O}_S)
              is local for the étale topology precisely if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_S(x)
              at every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x : Set \to S
              is a strictly
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henselian+ring"} Henselian
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+ring"} local ring
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, remark 4.4
            ).
          .un_prop
            %h6#example Example
            %ul
              %li
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+%C3%A9tale+topos"} little étale topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi et
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X_{et})
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+stack"} Deligne-Mumford stack
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is locally ringed with respect to the étale topology.
          %h3#abelian_tensor_categories Abelian tensor categories
          #AbelianTensorCategory.un_def
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong abelian tensor category
              (for the purposes of the present discusission) is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C, \otimes)
              such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  is an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              %li
                %p
                  for every
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in C
                  the functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) \otimes x : C\to C
                  is additive and right-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"}> exact
                  \: it commutes with finite
                  = succeed "s." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %p
              A
              %strong complete abelian tensor category
              is an abelian tensor category such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  it satisfies the axiom AB5 at
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+and+abelian+categories"} additive and abelian categories
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) \otimes x
                  commutes with
                  %em all small
                  colimits.
                %p
                  (equivalently, we have a
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
            %p
              An abelian tensor category is called
              %strong tame
              if for any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                    %mo ″
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to M'\to M \to M''\to 0
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ″
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M''
              a
              %em flat object
              (such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi M
                    %mo ″
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto x \otimes M''
              is an
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \in C
              also the induced sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                    %mo ″
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to M'\otimes N \to M\otimes N \to M''\otimes N \to 0
            %p is exact.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, def. 5.2
            ) together with the paragraph below remark 5.3.
          #TCAbTens.un_def
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C,D
              two
              %a{:href => "#AbelianTensorCategory"} complete abelian tensor categories
              write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Func
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Func_\otimes(C,D) \subset Func(C,D)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
              on those
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  are
                  = succeed "s;" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+functor"} symmetric monoidal functor
              %li
                %p
                  commute with all small
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+functor"} additive
                  and
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} right exact
              %li
                %p preserve flat objects and short exact sequences whose last object is flat.
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi TCAbTens
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    TCAbTens
            %p
              for the (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"}> strict
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
              of
              %a{:href => "#AbelianTensorCategory"} tame complete abelian tensor categories
              with hom-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"}> groupoid
              s given by this
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Func
                        %mo ⊗
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func_\otimes
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, def 5.9
            ) together with the following remarks.
          .un_lemma
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k Mod
              for its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\mathcal{O}_S)
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+topos"} ringed topos
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O}_S Mod
            %p
              (the category of sheaves of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_S
              = succeed "s)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#AbelianTensorCategory"} complete abelian tensor category
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, example 5.7
            ).
          .un_lemma
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+stack"} algebraic stack
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    QC(X)
            %p
              for its category
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaves"} quasicoherent sheaves
            %p
              This is a
              %a{:href => "#AbelianTensorCategory"} complete abelian tensor category
          .un_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a Noetherian geometric stack, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC(X)
              is the category of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-object"} ind-object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Coh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Coh(X) \subset QC(X)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Coh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    QC(X) \simeq Ind(Coh(X))
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, lemma 3.9
            ).
          %h3#GeometricStack Geometric stacks
          #geometricStack.un_def
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+stack"} geometric stack
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+stack"} algebraic stack
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Spec
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec \mathbb{Z}
              %li
                %p
                  that is quasi-compact, in particular there is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Spec
                          %mi A
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A \to X
              %li
                %p
                  with affine and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+morphism+of+stacks"} representable
                  diagonal
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X \times X
          .un_prop
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  A quasicompact
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated+scheme"} separated scheme
                  is a geometric stack.
              %li
                %p
                  The classifying stack of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+scheme"} smooth
                  affine
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
                  is a geometric stack.
          %p
            The geometricity condition on an algebraic stack implies that there are “enough”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaves"} quasicoherent sheaves
            on it, as formalized by the following statement.
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a{:href => "#geometricStack"} geometric stack
              then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+chain+complex"} bounded-below
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaves"} quasicoherent sheaves
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is naturally
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              of the left-bounded derived category of smooth-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+site"} etale
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+cohomology"} chain cohomology
              sheaves are quasicoherent.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, theorem 3.8
            ).
          %h2#tannaka_duality_for_geometric_stacks Tannaka duality for geometric stacks
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#GeometricStack"} geometric stack
            %p
              Then for every ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              there is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RngdTopos
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    RngdTopos(Sh((Spec A)_{et}),Sh(X_{et})) \simeq Hom_\otimes(QC(X), A Mod)
            %p
              hence (by the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-Yoneda+lemma"} 2-Yoneda lemma
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X(Spec A) \simeq Hom_\otimes(QC(X), QC(Spec A))
                    \\,.
            %p
              More generally, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S, \mathcal{O}_S)
              any
              %a{:href => "#localWRTEtaleTopology"} etale-locally
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+topos"} ringed topos
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi RngdTopos
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    RngdTopos(S,Sh(X_{et})) \simeq Hom_\otimes(QC(X), \mathcal{O}_S Mod)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, theorem 5.11
            ) in view of (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, remark 4.5
            ).
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              It follows that forming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaves"} quasicoherent sheaves
              constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} full and faithful (2,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QC
                    %mo :
                    %mi GeomStacks
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi TCAbTens
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    QC : GeomStacks \to TCAbTens^{op}
            %p
              from geometric stacks to
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#TCAbTens"} tame complete abelian tensor categories
            %p
              This statement justifies thinking of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC(X)
              as being the “2-algebra” of functions on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+noncommutative+geometry"} derived noncommutative geometry
